# Smoke tests of the pre-packed weights of the rv64 GEMM (jit:rvv), on small
# problems at their edges: N tails, N below one strip, broadcast and per-batch
# weights, bias and post-ops, the transposed tag, and thread partitions over M
# and K.

--reset
--impl=jit:rvv
--dt=f32,f16,bf16,s8:s8:s32,u8:s8:f32,s8:s8:s8
--stag=any --dtag=any --wtag=any,abx
64x300:300x77
5x1000:1000x130
96x700:700x264
130x40:40x515
1x17:17x15
4x20x260:1x260x150
3x31x300:3x300x70
2x2x9x40:2x1x40x65

# Bias and post-ops with packed weights
--reset
--impl=jit:rvv
--dt=f32
--wtag=any
--bia-dt=f32 --bia_mask=2
--attr-post-ops=,relu+add:f32:per_oc
64x300:300x77
4x20x260:1x260x150

# The 2D transposed tag stays on the plain path
--reset
--impl=jit:rvv
--dt=f32,s8:s8:s32
--wtag=ba
64x300:300x77

# Thread partitions over M (the weights' N) and K, aligned to panels
--reset
--impl=jit:rvv
--dt=f32,f16,s8:s8:s32
--wtag=any
16x256:256x2000
8x4000:4000x300
3x9x5000:1x5000x333
